erms of  basic visuals like I said Final Cut Pro  is what I use to edit and due to the  sheer amount of just content you know  pitches videos all this stuff that I use  in a typical video most of my projects  end up looking like what you currently  see on screen throughout the video I'll  use a lot of effects which can be found  over here in Final Cut Pro and in  between clips I'll typically use  transitions which can be found over here  again if you want to learn about how to  use this stuff in action then there are  many tutorials out there but for the  most part I think you'll find it quite  straightforward once you get started  Final Cut Pro comes with a ton of  effects so if you're not picky then I'm  sure there'll be something for whatever  you're thinking of but in my case you  know I was using them for a while and I  got a bit bored so I bought two  additional plugins that I've purchased  for Final Cut and these were made by a  company called pixel film studios the  main thing that I bought from them that  I use the most often is the cartoon mega  pack and this allows me to do epic  hand-drawn transitions like this one and  this one and that one but not to mention  you get random effects that aren't  really transitions they're just things  you can throw in the video anywhere and  I've done this for about two more  now I reckon two or three months and I  gotta say it was definitely worth the  cost for me as I basically use it in  every video that I've made since then  however I'm not saying that this is  something you need to get because  honestly most of my videos on YouTube do  not have any effects like this my  channel was still able to grow so I  would say it's not necessary but if you  think it will add value then yeah  definitely try it out  the other thing that I got from pixel  Studios was an audio visualizer package  what this allows me to do is that in  certain videos like the one you're  currently watching  whenever I'm speaking the the audio that 